# Allowlist for scripts/check_accidentals.py
#
# One entry per line: "<path>: <xml:id of the note>". An entry covers every
# report on that note. Only notes whose accidentals are knowingly left as they
# are belong here, each explained by the comment above it. The checker reports
# entries that no longer match a report, so remove an entry once it is fixed.

# --- No. 24, music example 1 (§ 17) -----------------------------------------
# The example demonstrates the old use of a flat to cancel a sharp, so the
# flats (sounding a natural) are kept in the modernised view, too.
encodings/24/mattheson/music-example1.xml: ex-n23u287
encodings/24/mattheson/music-example1.xml: ex-ngc9bwg
encodings/24/mattheson/music-example1.xml: ex-n9z96h3

# --- No. 4, realisation by J.-C. Dijoux -----------------------------------------
# A modern edition encoded in MEI Basic, which has no editorial markup: the
# cautionary accidentals the rules suggest cannot be supplied, and the file
# has no modernised view.
encodings/4/jcd/score.xml: *

# --- No. 15, aria, bar 85: the later printing of 1731 ---------------------------
# The later printing (#secondEditionReprint) sets the whole note a step higher, as
# f'' with the flat still before it; in that reading the f'' of bar 86 would want a
# courtesy natural, which the later printing does not print either.
encodings/15/mattheson/aria-bottari.xml: note-0000001778250400
